<title>HONG KONG: Hana Bank mandates US$100 million FRN.</title>
<headline>Hana Bank mandates US$100 million FRN.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-11-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hana Bank has mandated five banks to arrange a US$100 million floating rate note issue, bankers said.</p>
<p>They said the facility has a final maturity of five years with a put and a call option in year three.</p>
<p>The issue is likely to be priced at par to float at 31.5 basis points over the six-month London Interbank Offered Rate.</p>
<p>With fees, the all-in return for top-tier managers is expected to be around 36.5 basis points.</p>
<p>Arrangers are Citicorp International, DKB Asia, Dresdner SEA, IBJ Asia and Banca Nationale Del Lavoro.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2847 4039</p>
